Playa
-----

Source: https://github.com/dhdaines/playa
Oracle identity: compat/upstream.toml is the sole authoritative definition
of the oracle package, version, tag, and source commit.
Relationship and files: portions of the Go implementation derive from Playa,
with Go adaptations across document/, parser/, fontdata/, the public domain
packages, and cmd/playa/. compat/manifest.toml and docs/api-audit.md map the
compared behavior and public APIs to their Playa counterparts. The oracle is
a development/compatibility dependency, not a Python runtime requirement for
the Go library.
License: MIT. Full terms are retained in LICENSE and mirrored in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, "Playa license".
Retained attribution: David Huggins-Daines <dhd@ecolingui.ca>.

