Core 14 AFM inputs
-----------------

Original source: https://www.adobe.com/devnet/font/pdfs/Core14_AFMs.zip
Mirror: https://github.com/tecnickcom/tc-font-core14-afms
Authoritative local inputs: the 14 *.afm files and LICENSE under
scripts/data/core14/. scripts/sync_core14_afm.py refreshes from mirror main
without recording an immutable upstream commit.
Relationship and outputs: synchronization normalizes line endings and
trailing whitespace while preserving AFM semantics and notices. Each
synchronized AFM prominently records that normalization in a Comment.
Generators translate the metrics into fontdata/standard_metrics_generated.go and the
Symbol/ZapfDingbats data into fontdata/symbol_encoding_generated.go and
fontdata/zapfdingbats_encoding_generated.go. Per-file source notices and the
accompanying distribution terms remain in scripts/data/core14/.
License identifier: custom Adobe Core 14 AFM distribution terms (not MIT).
Full terms: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, "Core 14 AFM distribution terms" and
"Core 14 AFM per-font notices"; scripts/data/core14/LICENSE accompanies the
14 retained AFM files.
Specification reference: Adobe Technical Note #5004,
https://adobe-type-tools.github.io/font-tech-notes/pdfs/5004.AFM_Spec.pdf

PDF WinAnsi and MacRoman mapping references
------------------------------------------

Reference: ISO 32000-1:2008 Annex D.2,
https://opensource.adobe.com/dc-acrobat-sdk-docs/standards/pdfstandards/pdf/PDF32000_2008.pdf
Authority and outputs: scripts/generate_winansi_encoding.py and
scripts/generate_macroman_encoding.py generate
fontdata/winansi_encoding_generated.go and
fontdata/macroman_encoding_generated.go from Python codec mappings and PDF
glyph-assignment rules for space, hyphen, unused-code bullets, and currency.
No specification text or Python codec implementation is redistributed.
These generators use the reference to determine mapping behavior; the
project's original generator code is covered by LICENSE.

Optional public PDF corpora
--------------------------

The downloaded public PDFs are explicitly outside the distributed Go module.
They are fetched without content modification for compatibility tests and
benchmarks into .compat-cache/. They retain their own licenses, embedded
notices, and third-party credits; the project MIT license does not cover them.

Large-document sources:
- RISC-V Unprivileged Architecture, CC-BY-4.0:
  https://docs.riscv.org/
- OpenIntro Statistics, CC-BY-SA-3.0:
  https://www.openintro.org/book/os/
- GNU Emacs Manual, GFDL-1.3-or-later with invariant sections and cover texts:
  https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/
Authority: compat/public_corpus.json records publisher/download URLs,
document editions, exact sizes and SHA-256 hashes, attribution, license URLs,
and embedded-notice evidence. Preserve the GNU manual's identified invariant
sections and front/back-cover notices when redistributing that document.
Full terms: the per-document license_url entries and the downloaded documents'
embedded notices; these optional documents are not bundled here.

PDF Association sources:
- pdf20examples, CC-BY-SA-4.0:
  https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf20examples
- pdf-differences test files, CC-BY-4.0:
  https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-differences
- SafeDocs, Apache-2.0:
  https://github.com/pdf-association/safedocs
- techniques-for-accessible-pdf, CC-BY-4.0:
  https://github.com/pdf-association/techniques-for-accessible-pdf
Authority: internal/testfixture/pdf_association_fixtures.json records source
commits, fixture paths, content hashes, evidence, and full-license links.
cmd/playa-fixtures fetches those pinned sources; the PDFs are not redistributed
in the module. Full terms: the manifest's license_url entries and each
downloaded source's original notices.

